title: Powers
---
Lyre prays to the shrine she once built herself. Despite it being overrun by cables, she is granted an answer.
Istaya: Lyre.
Istaya: I require your aid. Urgently.
Lyre: I don’t suppose you have an answer to my earlier question, then?
Istaya: You’ve taken note of the visitors, yes?
Lyre: They’re hard to miss.
Istaya: I cannot rid myself of them. They are unresponsive.
Istaya: My strategies keep them unphased, there is no empathy in their minds.
Istaya: I cannot resonate with feelings that are not present. So they remain.
Istaya: Lyre.
Istaya: You need to convey to them that they are unwelcome.
Lyre: And now exactly are you proposing I do that?
Lyre: Do enlighten me.
Istaya: Let me open your third eye.
Istaya: With it, I can grant you the perception of one of my visitors.
Istaya: Let it know they are living on borrowed time.
Lyre: ...
Lyre: I have a counteroffer.
Istaya: Choose your next words carefully, child. You are in no position to make demands.
Lyre: You will open my third eye.
Lyre: However, I will choose my own methods to rid you of these robots.
Lyre: And you are not to intervene.
Istaya: ...
Istaya: Please close your eyes.
===
